questions.questionTextEn:
What is the maximum recursion depth (number of simultaneous active stack frames) when calling `f(10)` for:
```c
int f(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return f(n - 2) + f(n - 2);
}
```

Consider the recursive function on a singly linked list:
```c
struct Node* rev(struct Node* head) {
    if (!head || !head->next) return head;
    struct Node* rest = rev(head->next);
    head->next->next = head;
    head->next = NULL;
    return rest;
}
```
For a list of `n` nodes, what are the time complexity and auxiliary stack space complexity of `rev`?
